WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.490
Israel, about 760 BCE.

2
00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:06.660
A wealthy kingdom, busy
sanctuaries at Bethel,

3
00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:08.710
and a prophet called Amos.

4
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.480
First he condemns the
neighbours: Damascus,

5
00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:14.960
Gaza, Tyre, Edom, Ammon, Moab.

6
00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:16.580
His listeners cheer.

7
00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:17.670
Then Judah.

8
00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:21.040
Then, last and longest, Israel itself.

9
00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:25.890
And Amos claims God chose only Israel,
and therefore will punish them.

10
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.860
Why would being chosen make
punishment worse, not lighter?

11
00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:33.650
In this mission, you'll hear his
charges against the rich of Samaria,

12
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.210
and a day everyone was longing for.

13
00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:40.930
Then you'll weigh up whether his demands
still speak in a world of many values.

14
00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:46.290
Your mission: find out why, for Amos,
being chosen made punishment worse.
